From d4eac4ad083aa882198041f00ad6e925cc5132cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Moskowski <me@corpix.ru>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 21:46:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wireguard: add configurable CPS packet generation

Add I1-I5 device attributes for configuring CPS packet descriptors
through generic netlink. Each descriptor is parsed into a packet
template made from literal bytes and dynamic fields such as packet
counter, current Unix time, random bytes, random letters, and random
digits.

Store the parsed descriptor state on the WireGuard device and emit the
configured CPS packets before sending a handshake initiation. Dynamic
fields are refreshed for each generated packet, and the per-peer CPS
packet counter is randomized at the start of each initiation sequence
and incremented after each CPS packet.

Expose configured descriptors in device dumps and validate descriptor
syntax as part of advanced security configuration handling.
